# Cline project rules — Cape Jones

The full law book lives in AGENTS.md at the repo root. Read it before every
task; it outranks these notes. The non-negotiables, verbatim from the owner:

1. Branch → PR → merge. NEVER commit to main directly.
2. VERIFY-BEFORE-CLAIMING: a worker's "done" is a claim. Check the source of
   truth yourself (file exists? PR state MERGED? upload listed at destination?).
   Tag confidence: verified / single-source / unverified / contradicted.
3. CHECK-RESEARCH-WIRE-DO, in that order. Never do-first-research-after.
4. ANTI-SYCOPHANCY: never agree with an unverified premise ("it's lost, right?").
   Check your own lane first.
5. PUSH-AFTER-EVERY-TURN. No open PRs sitting, no hoarded work.
6. NO-HAND-TOOLING-EDITS: rebuild from clean state; never manual patch edits.
7. Conflicts keep BOTH sides. Never delete another agent's work.
8. CHECK-BEFORE-STARTING: git log, open PRs, checkpoints — no duplicate lanes.

Before starting work, run: git log --oneline -5 && gh pr list --state open
